<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Frame on brainboxemb</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/frame/</link><description>Recent content in Frame on brainboxemb</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/frame/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Aluminium Frame Design Considerations</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/frame/aluminium-frame/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/frame/aluminium-frame/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The internal frame uses 20 × 20 mm aluminium construction profiles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="main-dimensions"&gt;Main dimensions&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
	&lt;thead&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Dimension&lt;/th&gt;
					&lt;th style="text-align: right"&gt;Value&lt;/th&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/thead&gt;
	&lt;tbody&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Overall width&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;840 mm&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Overall height&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;360 mm&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Horizontal profiles&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;840 mm&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Vertical profiles&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;320 mm&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Profile size&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;20 × 20 mm&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The overall height consists of a 20 mm top profile, a 320 mm vertical profile and a 20 mm bottom profile.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="panel-mounting"&gt;Panel mounting&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The five HUB75 panels will be mounted to the frame using custom brackets.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Aluminium Extrusion Frame Idea</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/frame/aluminium-extrusion-frame/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/frame/aluminium-extrusion-frame/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Aluminium extrusion could be used to create a rigid and modular frame around the LED panels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.instructables.com/Simple-Extruded-Aluminum-Frame-for-LED-Panels/"&gt;Simple Extruded Aluminum Frame for LED Panels&lt;/a&gt; — practical example of constructing an LED-panel frame using aluminium extrusion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://hackaday.com/2021/02/23/useful-build-tips-for-making-led-panel-frames/"&gt;Useful Build Tips for Making LED Panel Frames&lt;/a&gt; — notes about measurements, magnetic mounting, wiring, DIN rail, controller mounting and power supplies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
